<title>AUSTRALIA: BZW confirms St George A$300 mln bond.</title>
<headline>BZW confirms St George A$300 mln bond.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>BZW Australia confirmed that it has lead managed a A$300 million domestic bond issue for St George Bank on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds, which mature July 15, 1999, carry a coupon of 6.1 percent, and were priced at 36 basis points over the July 1999 government bond to yield 6.215 percent, a BZW official said.</p>
<p>St George is co-manager to the issue, which is rated A by S&amp;P and A3 by Moody's. Settlement date is June 6.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
